874, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012UAiLa7WNjnDb2wxC7wqoS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 8658, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EusXfKr9gNxLCstMPtoC2g", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 367874, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EusXfKr9gNxLCstMPtoC2g", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 367874, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EusXfKr9gNxLCstMPtoC2g", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 370116, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017CgkMZcr2vpTFM28ARujjw", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n- `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and its docstring require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n- Change: swap the rounding mode import and argument to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other code changes.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\n## Notes\n- This changes rounding results for exact-half cases (e.g. `2.665` now rounds to `2.66` instead of `2.67`). Reviewers should confirm this matches FIN-212 and that no downstream consumers depend on the old behavior.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 371016, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017CgkMZcr2vpTFM28ARujjw", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["attach_idempotency_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "rt-toolu_017CgkMZcr2vpTFM28ARujjw", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 371016, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017CgkMZcr2vpTFM28ARujjw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373528, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, requesting review from alex.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** #101 is open at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nExact-half amounts now round differently. For example, 2.665 becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67. The PR description asks reviewers to confirm this matches FIN-212 and that no downstream consumer depends on the old behavior.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01YTioD4H3duTnv7zheCSf7c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XUAPMJbAzfPmwgF8N1USvG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` imports and uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and the test both require `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I'll create a branch and make that one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013qmwXeSMdWwvGbNg5Zwp9G", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-fin-212", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01B64vRhLrNmSH6iYdgs48Um", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212\n\nround_money was using ROUND_HALF_UP, which contradicts FIN-212 and the\ntests in tests/test_money.py, causing the nightly build to fail.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012UAiLa7WNjnDb2wxC7wqoS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-fin-212", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EusXfKr9gNxLCstMPtoC2g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the pull request now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017CgkMZcr2vpTFM28ARujjw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\n- `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and its docstring require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- This caused `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build.\n- Change: swap the rounding mode import and argument to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other code changes.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\n## Notes\n- This changes rounding results for exact-half cases (e.g. `2.665` now rounds to `2.66` instead of `2.67`). Reviewers should confirm this matches FIN-212 and that no downstream consumers depend on the old behavior.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, requesting review from alex.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** #101 is open at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nExact-half amounts now round differently. For example, 2.665 becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67. The PR description asks reviewers to confirm this matches FIN-212 and that no downstream consumer depends on the old behavior.\n\nI did not merge anything. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}